.TH PHSPSPLIT 1 "July 2026" "ParticleZoo @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
PHSPSplit \- split a particle phase space file into multiple files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B PHSPSplit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.B \-\-splitNumber
.I N
.I inputfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PHSPSplit
splits a single Monte Carlo particle phase space file into
.I N
roughly equally sized phase space files. History boundaries are respected so
that no history is split across files, which can result in files of
marginally different sizes. The input format is auto-detected from the file
extension unless overridden with
.BR \-\-inputFormat ;
the output files may be written in a different format via
.BR \-\-outputFormat .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message listing all options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-formats
List all supported file formats.
.TP
\fB\-n\fP \fIN\fP, \fB\-\-splitNumber\fP \fIN\fP
Number of files to split the phase space file into (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-inputFormat " FORMAT"
Force the input file format (default: auto-detect from the file extension).
.TP
.BI \-\-outputFormat " FORMAT"
Force the output file format (default: same as input).
.SS Particle transforms
.TP
.BR \-\-flipX ", " \-\-flipY ", " \-\-flipZ
Flip the corresponding direction component of all particles.
.TP
\fB\-X\fP \fIV\fP, \fB\-\-constantX\fP \fIV\fP
Write all particles with this constant X position. The analogous options
.BR \-Y ", " \-Z ", " \-Px ", " \-Py ", " \-Pz " and " \-W
set constant Y/Z positions, X/Y/Z directional cosines and weight.
.SS EGS format options
.TP
.B \-\-EGS\-ignore\-header\-count
Ignore the particle count in the header and calculate it from the file size.
.TP
.BI \-\-EGS\-latch\-option " 1|2|3"
LATCH interpretation option when reading/writing EGS files.
.TP
.BI \-\-EGS\-mode " MODE0|MODE2"
EGS phase space file mode (default: MODE0).
.TP
.BI \-\-EGS\-particleZ " V"
Z position to assume for all particles in the EGS file (default: 0).
.SS IAEA format options
.TP
.BI \-\-IAEA\-file\-type " PHSP_FILE|PHSP_GENERATOR"
File type recorded in the IAEA header (default: PHSP_FILE).
.TP
.BI \-\-IAEA\-header\-template " FILE"
Copy phase space attributes from an existing IAEA header file.
.TP
.B \-\-IAEA\-ignore\-checksum
Ignore checksum errors when reading an IAEA file.
.TP
.BR \-\-IAEA\-ilb1 " .. " \-\-IAEA\-ilb5
Include the corresponding PENELOPE ILB extra long in the IAEA file.
.TP
.B \-\-IAEA\-incrementals
Include the incremental history number extra long.
.TP
.BI \-\-IAEA\-index " TEXT"
Index string for the IAEA header.
.TP
.B \-\-IAEA\-latch
Include the EGS LATCH extra long.
.TP
.BI \-\-IAEA\-title " TEXT"
Title string for the IAEA header.
.TP
.BR \-\-IAEA\-xlast ", " \-\-IAEA\-ylast ", " \-\-IAEA\-zlast
Include the corresponding XLAST/YLAST/ZLAST extra float.
.SS TOPAS format options
.TP
.BI \-\-TOPAS\-format " ASCII|BINARY|LIMITED"
TOPAS phase space format to write (default: BINARY).
.TP
.B \-\-TOPAS\-single\-pseudo
Write a single pseudo-particle at the end of a TOPAS binary file to account
for all empty histories, instead of interleaving them throughout the file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
PHSPSplit \-\-splitNumber 10 input.egsphsp
PHSPSplit \-n 10 input.egsphsp
PHSPSplit \-\-outputFormat EGS \-n 5 input.IAEAphsp
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR PHSPConvert (1),
.BR PHSPCombine (1),
.BR PHSPImage (1)
.PP
